{
  "id": "1CH.18",
  "number": "18",
  "bookId": "1CH",
  "reference": "1 Chronicles 18",
  "verseCount": 17,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "18",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "1CH 18"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "18",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Some time later King David attacked the Philistines again and defeated them. He took out of their control the city of Gath and its surrounding villages. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He also defeated the Moabites, who became his subjects and paid taxes to him.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.2"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Next, David attacked King Hadadezer of the Syrian state of Zobah, near the territory of Hamath, because Hadadezer was trying to gain control of the territory by the upper Euphrates. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "David captured a thousand of his chariots, 7,000 horsemen, and 20,000 foot soldiers. He kept enough horses for a hundred chariots and crippled all the rest.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.4"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When the Syrians of Damascus sent an army to help King Hadadezer, David attacked it and killed 22,000 men. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then he set up military camps in their territory, and they became his subjects and paid taxes to him. The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " made David victorious everywhere. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "David captured the gold shields carried by Hadadezer's officials and took them to Jerusalem. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "1KI.7.40+1KI.7.41+1KI.7.42+1KI.7.43+1KI.7.44+1KI.7.45+1KI.7.46+1KI.7.47"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "1 Kgs 7.40–47",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "2CH.4.11+2CH.4.12+2CH.4.13+2CH.4.14+2CH.4.15+2CH.4.16+2CH.4.17+2CH.4.18"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "2 Chr 4.11–18",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He also took a great quantity of bronze from Tibhath and Kun, cities ruled by Hadadezer. (Solomon later used this bronze to make the tank, the columns, and the bronze utensils for the Temple.)",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.8"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "King Toi of Hamath heard that David had defeated Hadadezer's entire army. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So he sent his son Joram to greet King David and congratulate him for his victory over Hadadezer, against whom Toi had fought many times. Joram brought David presents made of gold, silver, and bronze. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "King David dedicated them for use in worship, along with the silver and gold he took from the nations he conquered — Edom, Moab, Ammon, Philistia, and Amalek.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.11"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "PSA.60"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Ps 60",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "(Title)",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Abishai, whose mother was Zeruiah, defeated the Edomites in the Valley of Salt and killed 18,000 of them. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He set up military camps throughout Edom, and the people there became King David's subjects. The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " made David victorious everywhere.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.13"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "David ruled over all Israel and made sure that his people were always treated fairly and justly. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Abishai's brother Joab was commander of the army; Jehoshaphat son of Ahilud was in charge of the records; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Zadok son of Ahitub and Ahimelech son of Abiathar were priests; Seraiah",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18.16",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Probable text (see 2 Sam 8.17)",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Seraiah",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "; Hebrew",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Shavsha.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " was court secretary; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 18:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Benaiah son of Jehoiada was in charge of David's bodyguard; and King David's sons held high positions in his service.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.18.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.18.17"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "next": {
    "id": "1CH.19",
    "number": "19",
    "bookId": "1CH"
  },
